{"type":"message","id":"3e835a09","parentId":"338b87aa","timestamp":"2026-06-01T13:26:26.213Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking which config options affect memory formation. Let me get the current actual config to see what's actually set, and also look at the workspace path from AGENTS.md which shows where memory files live.\n\nLet me now give a clear summary of the config options that affect memory, based on what I've found:\n\n1. `memory.backend` - builtin vs qmd\n2. `memory.citations` - whether to show citations\n3. `session.scope` - per-sender vs global\n4. `session.dmScope` - how DM sessions are scoped\n5. `session.resetTriggers` - phrases that reset session\n6. `session.maintenance` - pruning/cleanup settings\n\n\n7. `session.store` - where sessions are persisted\n8. `session.writeLock` - controls how transcripts are written and locked\n\nThe workspace path is `/home/node/.openclaw/workspace`, and that's where AGENTS.md defines the memory files like `MEMORY.md`, `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`, and `HEARTBEAT.md`. I should also check if there's a project context path configured elsewhere.\n","thinkingSignature":"95c2e6502fd26b56076f6c0038d3197b0871fd0e98e4719877dfd6bef09d7c1a"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_yixj21v99w0k_1","name":"gateway","arguments":{"action":"config.get"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":3967,"output":255,"cacheRead":27205,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":31427,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780320377852,"responseId":"066cbb7af2ddbee5df16da6f66df9114"}}
