{"type":"message","id":"ce2577b0","parentId":"4e6c299e","timestamp":"2026-06-01T15:10:15.608Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants to know if memory_search is working properly in the current config. Let me check the memorySearch configuration more carefully, especially the provider and model details.\n\nFrom what I saw earlier:\n```json\n\"memorySearch\": {\n  \"enabled\": true,\n  \"provider\": \"gemini\",\n  \"model\": \"text-embedding-004\"\n}\n```\n\nBut I also saw in agents.defaults.memorySearch it uses \"gemini\" as provider with text-embedding-004. Let me check if this is properly configured - the google provider needs to be enabled and have the right API key.\n\nAlso let me check what \"provider\" means here - is it referring to a plugin or a model provider? From the config, I saw \"google\" in plugins.allow and plugins.entries - and the google provider in models.providers has `gemini-2.5-flash` etc.\n \nNow I'm looking at the actual configuration more carefully - the memorySearch is using provider \"gemini\" with model \"text-embedding-004\", but I need to verify if this \"gemini\" provider is actually available in the models.providers list or if it's supposed to be \"google\" instead.\n\nThe plugins.allow array includes \"google\", so the google plugin should be enabled, but I'm not certain whether the memory_search tool actually routes through the plugins system or calls the Google API directly. The fact that config.get was failing before suggests there might be an issue with how the configuration is being loaded or validated.\n\nLet me think through the actual setup: the provider is set to \"gemini\" but the models.providers section only defines \"google\" - there might be a mismatch between what memorySearch expects and what's actually configured.\n\nI should check if \"google\" in plugins.allow actually corresponds to a \"gemini\" provider that the memorySearch tool can use, or if I need to reconfigure the memorySearch section to use \"google\" instead of \"gemini\".\n","thinkingSignature":"95e61133398bc40f3d629ace1e7c3a44050f7325bccf831928956fceb4341cd5"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_85vw60oclomy_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json | python3 -c \"\nimport json, sys\nd = json.load(sys.stdin)\n\nprint('=== memorySearch ===')\nms = d.get('agents',{}).get('defaults',{}).get('memorySearch',{})\nprint(json.dumps(ms, indent=2))\n\nprint()\nprint('=== google plugin enabled? ===')\nplugins = d.get('plugins',{})\nallow = plugins.get('allow',[])\nentries = plugins.get('entries',{})\nprint('allow:', allow)\nprint('google entry:', json.dumps(entries.get('google','不存在'), indent=2))\n\nprint()\nprint('=== models.providers.google ===')\ngoogle = d.get('models',{}).get('providers',{}).get('google',{})\nprint(json.dumps(google, indent=2))\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":2743,"output":590,"cacheRead":44161,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":47494,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780326603518,"responseId":"066cd3cc2ee1c819f9efe8150f7557e2"}}
{"type":"message","id":"36eb3c3b","parentId":"ce2577b0","timestamp":"2026-06-01T15:10:15.898Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_85vw60oclomy_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== memorySearch ===\n{\n  \"enabled\": true,\n  \"provider\": \"gemini\",\n  \"model\": \"text-embedding-004\"\n}\n\n=== google plugin enabled? ===\nallow: ['duckduckgo', 'feishu', 'google', 'memory-core', 'minimax', 'nvidia', 'openclaw-weixin', 'tavily', 'volcengine', 'zai']\ngoogle entry: {\n  \"enabled\": true\n}\n\n=== models.providers.google ===\n{\n  \"baseUrl\": \"https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai\",\n  \"api\": \"openai-completions\",\n  \"models\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"gemini-2.5-flash-lite\",\n      \"name\": \"Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite\",\n      \"api\": \"openai-completions\",\n      \"reasoning\": false,\n      \"input\": [\n        \"text\",\n        \"image\"\n      ],\n      \"cost\": {\n        \"input\": 0,\n        \"output\": 0,\n        \"cacheRead\": 0,\n        \"cacheWrite\": 0\n      },\n      \"contextWindow\": 1000000,\n      \"maxTokens\": 65536\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"gemini-2.5-flash\",\n      \"name\": \"Gemini 2.5 Flash\",\n      \"api\": \"openai-completions\",\n      \"reasoning\": false,\n      \"input\": [\n        \"text\",\n        \"image\"\n      ],\n      \"cost\": {\n        \"input\": 0,\n        \"output\": 0,\n        \"cacheRead\": 0,\n        \"cacheWrite\": 0\n      },\n      \"contextWindow\": 1000000,\n      \"maxTokens\": 65536\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":120,"aggregated":"=== memorySearch ===\n{\n  \"enabled\": true,\n  \"provider\": \"gemini\",\n  \"model\": \"text-embedding-004\"\n}\n\n=== google plugin enabled? ===\nallow: ['duckduckgo', 'feishu', 'google', 'memory-core', 'minimax', 'nvidia', 'openclaw-weixin', 'tavily', 'volcengine', 'zai']\ngoogle entry: {\n  \"enabled\": true\n}\n\n=== models.providers.google ===