{"type":"message","id":"9249a9eb","parentId":"e387d4ab","timestamp":"2026-06-01T15:21:55.501Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is saying that when I try to edit files, I frequently get a failure message like \"Edit: in ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json failed\" and then there's no follow-up. This is about my edit tool failures.\n\nLooking back at the conversation, I had two edit failures - one when I tried to edit the openclaw.json file and one when I tried to add the text-embedding-004 model. Both failed because the exact text matching didn't work due to truncation/redaction in the file output.\n\nThe issue is that when I read the file, certain sensitive values are redacted (like API keys show as `\"sk-or-…4fa9\"` instead of actual values), so when I try to match the text, it doesn't find the exact string because the actual content differs from what's shown to me.\n \nI see the problem now - the truncation and redaction in the file display is preventing me from finding exact text matches. For structured JSON files where I need to make precise insertions, I should switch to using exec with Python instead of relying on the edit tool's pattern matching.\n","thinkingSignature":"2ca563d868acc559a937fed0601a0e0fee61f98accc00669a77c669160060b1e"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n明白了。\n\n问题是 `edit` 工具要求**oldText 完全匹配文件原文**，但文件里有些内容被截断或脱敏了（比如 API key 显示成 `sk-or-…4fa9`），我看到的和实际内容不符，所以匹配不上。\n\n刚才那次我绕过去了——改用 Python exec 直接读写 JSON，但过程中还是会有隐式截断问题。\n\n**以后遇到 JSON 结构修改，用 Python 做更稳妥。**\n\n需要我重启 gateway 使 text-embedding-004 生效吗？还是先不做？"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":2875,"output":331,"cacheRead":48749,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":51955,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780327306912,"responseId":"066cd68b89d665bfbe7230f4f2b30d40"}}
