{"type":"message","id":"e384765f","parentId":"f05c9ad2","timestamp":"2026-06-01T15:38:50.753Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Based on what I found, I can give the user a meaningful upgrade analysis. Key findings:\n\n1. The user is on 2026.5.19, wants to upgrade to 2026.5.28 (which is actually 2026.5.31 based on the release page - there might not be a 2026.5.28 stable release, only beta)\n\n2. Looking at the changelog, there are no explicit \"breaking changes\" mentioned in either version. However, some things to note:\n\nFrom 2026.5.28 release notes:\n- Some behavior changes around session locks, hook context, workspace separation\n- Browser tool timeouts, viewport/tab indices stricter validation\n- Some provider model additions\n- Discord component ids stricter\n\nFrom 2026.5.31 (later beta):\n- SQLite-backed state for iMessage and other components\n- Cron retry behavior changes\n- Memory/QMD improvements\n\nSince the user is on 2026.5.19 and wants to go to 2026.5.28, and the `lastTouchedVersion` in their config says 2026.5.19, they're relatively current. But 2026.5.28 might not actually exist as a stable release - looking at the GitHub page, the latest stable seems to be around 2026.5.31-beta.\n\nLet me check what version is actually latest stable vs beta.\n","thinkingSignature":"fd5933817a39a998bcc24c74d76a646cc294c0d4224b21f9733da883fb4740b3"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_midrsz5e07lo_1","name":"web_fetch","arguments":{"maxChars":3000,"url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/releases/latest"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":3174,"output":340,"cacheRead":57371,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":60885,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780328322249,"responseId":"066cda8230153e32963c4c09c25cf8d2"}}
