{"type":"message","id":"d8aaa12f","parentId":"24fb5d6c","timestamp":"2026-06-01T17:32:48.986Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The sessions look normal - they have reasonable sizes and are from different times. Let me check which session is the current one for this DM session (from sender ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff).Looking at the session key pattern from commands.log: `agent:main:feishu:main:direct:ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff`\n\nThe most recent session is fabd509d-37ba-4257-a417-d72fd9662362.jsonl (274714 bytes, updated Jun 1 17:31).\n\n\nThat session is quite large and appears to be actively receiving messages right now, which could suggest the gateway is processing but hasn't responded yet. But the user's actually reporting that group messages are stuck, not DM messages. Let me check the group chat sessions - the latest is d197434d-35fb-44bc-bc58-fc44042c8652.jsonl at 36245 bytes from Jun 1 17:15, though fabd509d might actually be the group session since it was updated at 17:31.\n\nI should look for sessions with a \"group\" chat type and check what feishu's polling/websocket logs show. The gateway's health endpoint is responding fine, so the service itself is running. The real question is whether it's actually receiving and processing messages from feishu. Since the feishu plugin uses websocket mode by default, that should handle real-time message receipt without issues. Let me check if there's a gateway log that shows incoming feishu messages.\n","thinkingSignature":"b6b1d7ccb72698f1524e3b93e8c9dee6a92b2720d776fa4797efa3ee94ce8558"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_k6n3vm2niars_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"ls -la /home/node/.openclaw/logs/ && find /home/node/.openclaw/logs/stability -type f 2>/dev/null | head -10","timeout":5}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":4349,"output":409,"cacheRead":71346,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":